    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1000">

                <pb facs="1130" n="986" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg986"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">884.05/6: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Southard</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-08-10T13:00:00-04:00">August 10, 1929—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>38. Reference your despatch No. 179, April 10.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d1000-f1"/>
                    While establishment in Ethiopia of a court having jurisdiction over foreign
                    nationals would, in principle, be agreeable to the Department, it believes the
                    proposal of the Diplomatic Corps at Addis Ababa needs further redrafting and
                    consideration.</p>
                <p>Prior to preparing definite instructions, the Department would like to be
                    informed of the attitude of the other powers interested. You should discreetly
                    endeavor to ascertain this from your colleagues.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cotton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
